    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output today, anchored by the premium efficiency of **Yordan Alvarez** (78.25), **Trea Turner** (77.18), and **Kyle Schwarber** (76.47). **Yordan Alvarez** remains the focal point of the lineup, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Chandler (4.27 xERA) and an elite xwOBA profile that justifies his position as our top play. Similarly, **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** enjoy a massive +18% SP skill boost against V\u00e1squez, whose elevated xERA of 4.75 makes him a primary target for our power-speed threats. While **Junior Caminero** (65.10) faces a tougher arm in Flaherty, his current form and lineup placement in the two-hole keep him firmly in the Strong recommendation tier.\n\nStrategic adjustments for today focus on capitalizing on platoon splits, specifically with **Christian Yelich** (54.28) and **Dillon Dingler** (56.09), both of whom receive double-digit efficiency bumps from their respective platoon advantages. The most difficult decision at the bottom of the order involved **Carson Benge** (42.20), who narrowly missed the starting cut; despite his upside, his efficiency was capped by a difficult matchup against Logan Gilbert (3.22 xERA), causing the optimizer to favor the higher baseline projections of **Jose Fernandez** (56.27) and **Caleb Durbin** (56.67). **Caleb Durbin** remains an essential start for our SB-starved rotation, as his matchup against Baz provides a high-leverage opportunity for stolen bases given the pitcher's slow delivery.\n\nRisks today are centered on two of our speed-dependent outfielders. **Luke Raley** (47.18) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (53.38) are facing elite defensive catchers with 1.89s pop times, which will likely neutralize their attempts to steal bases, a critical factor given our 5x5 scarcity requirements. Managers should monitor the lineup status for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Chase Meidroth** (59.14) closely, as their scores are contingent on staying in the top-of-order slots. While **Jacob Gonzalez** (36.44) and **Casey Schmitt** (38.32) were considered, they currently fall below our 40.0 efficiency floor and will remain benched to protect our game cap usage.",
